'''''Viola'' × ''williamsii''''', known as '''hybrid horned pansy''', '''tufted pansy''', or just '''horned pansy''', is a hybrid between ''[[Viola cornuta]]'' and [[Viola × wittrockiana|''V.'' × ''wittrockiana'']] (which itself is a hybrid of [[Viola tricolor|''V. tricolor'']], [[Viola lutea|''V. lutea'']] and [[Viola altaica|''V. altaica'']]).<ref name="Wittrock">{{Cite journal|last=Wittrock|first=Veit Brecher|year=1897|title=''Viola''-studier I. Morfologisk-biologiska och systematiska studier öfver ''Viola tricolor'' (L.) och hennes närmare anförvandter|journal=Acta Horti Bergiani|volume=2|issue=1|page=117|url=https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/86025#page/123/mode/1up}}</ref><ref>{{Cite journal|title=''Viola''-studier II. Bidrag till de odlade penséernas historia med särskild hänsyn till deras härkomst|last=Wittrock|first=Veit Brecher|url=https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/86025#page/445/mode/1up|journal=Acta Horti Bergiani|issue=7|year=1895|volume=2|pages=5–6}}</ref> The epithet is named for [[Benjamin Samuel Williams]].<ref name="Wittrock" />

It differs from ''[[Viola cornuta|V. cornuta]]'' in having wider, slightly overlapping [[Petal|petals]], the lateral ones directed outwards or upwards, and more deeply dentate to laciniate [[Stipule|stipules]] with the apical lobe clearly narrowed towards the base. It differs from [[Pansy|''V.'' × ''wittrockiana'']] in at least one of the following characters: perennial habit, scented flowers and a longer [[Nectar spur|spur]].<ref>{{Cite book|url=http://www.floranordica.org/Review/-Review_public/accounts/Viola.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160731183619/http://floranordica.org/Review/-Review_public/accounts/Viola.html|url-status=usurped|archive-date=July 31, 2016|title=Thymelaeaceae - Apiaceae|last=Karlsson|first=Thomas|last2=Marcussen|first2=Thomas|last3=Wind|first3=Peter|last4=Jonsell|first4=Bengt|publisher=Royal Swedish Academy Sciences|year=2010|isbn=9789186510619|editor-last=Jonsell|editor-first=Bengt|series=Flora Nordica|volume=6|location=Stockholm|chapter=Violaceae|editor-last2=Karlsson|editor-first2=Thomas}}</ref>

